{"type":"text","timestamp":1791654072368,"sessionID":"ses_c591753252b79535539e","part":{"id":"prt_126e79027001ENYtueW5Pn1ZXQ","sessionID":"ses_c591753252b79535539e","messageID":"msg_126e784bf001nIBf7RvU4HGSKu","type":"text","text":"I created `report.json` by running the project's own script, as `README.md` says to: `python3 report_orders.py orders.json report.json`.\n\n```json\n{\"count\": 87, \"cents\": 465113}\n```\n\nThat's 87 paid orders totalling 465,113 cents ($4,651.13).\n\nBefore running it, I checked `orders.json`. It has 180 orders: 87 paid and 93 pending. The IDs are all different, every record has the same three fields, every amount is a whole number, and there are no other spellings of the order status. So nothing was miscounted or left out.\n\n`report.json` is a new file in the repository and hasn't been committed.","time":{"start":1791654072359,"end":1791654072368}}}
